From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: V <61495413+kelo221@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 03:22:48 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Soloud::getApproximateVolume: channels past the engine's read
 0, not past the array

The channel was compared with `>` instead of `>=`, so channel 8 of an
8-channel engine read past mVisualizationChannelVolume (into the wave
data). Bus::getApproximateVolume had the same defect (patch 0047).
---
 src/core/soloud.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/core/soloud.cpp b/src/core/soloud.cpp
index 5cd5da0..26246a6 100644
--- a/src/core/soloud.cpp
+++ b/src/core/soloud.cpp
@@ -769,7 +769,7 @@ namespace SoLoud
 
 	float Soloud::getApproximateVolume(unsigned int aChannel)
 	{
-		if (aChannel > mChannels)
+		if (aChannel >= mChannels)
 			return 0;
 		float vol = 0;
 		lockAudioMutex_internal();
